{
  "title": "HumHub \u2014 social (6,685\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: HumHub\nDomain: social | Scale: large | Stars: 6,685\nProblem: Organizations need an open-source, self-hosted enterprise social network platform to enable internal communication, collaboration, and knowledge sharing. HumHub provides a modular, extensible intranet/social network solution that can be tailored to specific organizational needs.\nTarget users: Enterprise organizations, Intranet administrators, Non-profit organizations, Educational institutions, Community managers, Network operators\nCore features: User profiles with customizable fields, follow system, and permission management; Spaces (group rooms) for projects, departments, or events with advanced permissions; Content creation and sharing (posts, wiki, photos, videos, events, tasks); Modular architecture with ~80 installable/activatable modules; Notification system including email summaries; Multi-level commenting and collaboration tools; Search and filtering across content, spaces, and members; Multilingual support (30+ languages)\nIntegrations: LDAP / Advanced LDAP, RESTful API, OnlyOffice, JWT SSO, SMTP/Email\nTech stack: JavaScript, SCSS/CSS, Bootstrap (responsive) + PHP (Yii2 framework) + MySQL/MariaDB (Yii2 ActiveRecord) + Self-hosted (Apache/Nginx), Grunt-based asset pipeline\nKey libraries: Yii2, Grunt, grunt-contrib-less, grunt-contrib-uglify, grunt-contrib-cssmin, grunt-contrib-concat\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Modular monolith design via Yii2's module system allows extensibility without microservices complexity, enabling ~80 optional modules to be installed and activated independently.\n- Yii2 framework provides a structured MVC pattern with built-in RBAC, making enterprise-grade permission and role management more manageable at scale.\n- Grunt-based asset pipeline (LESS compilation, JS uglification, CSS minification) reflects a pre-modern frontend toolchain typical of PHP projects that predate Node-centric build systems.\n- AGPL-3.0 licensing combined with a commercial marketplace for premium modules is a deliberate open-core monetization strategy targeting enterprise customers.",
